### ============================================================
###  Projects API
###  Run auth.http first to populate {{access_token}}.
###  {{tenantId}} is set in http-client.env.json.
### ============================================================

### List visible projects (projects the caller has a ProjectMember row for)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Create a project
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "My First Project",
  "description": "Created via IntelliJ HTTP client"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("project_id", response.body.id);
  client.log("Created project: " + response.body.id);
%}

### Get a specific project (uses project_id from createProject above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{project_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### List members of a project
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{project_id}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Add a member to a project (caller must be tenant OWNER)
###   Replace USER_ID with the target user's Aran user id (from GET /api/me)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{project_id}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "userId": "REPLACE_WITH_TARGET_USER_ID"
}

### ── Error cases ────────────────────────────────────────────

### 404 — project that doesn't exist or isn't visible
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Accept: application/json

### 400 — blank project name (validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "description": "This should fail"
}

### 429 — rate limit (send this request >300 times quickly to trigger)
### Uncomment and run in a loop from the terminal instead:
### for i in {1..350}; do curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" \
###   -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" http://localhost:8081/api/projects; done
